      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Contours playground\n\nOne extraction, many queries. The photo is binarized (Otsu: light shapes on a dark background) and 'CV Find Contours' traces every blob once; each branch below asks the contour set a different question:\n\n- OUTLINE EVERYTHING: 'CV Draw Contours' paints all outlines.\n- FILTER BY PROPERTY: 'CV Filter Contours' keeps the round shapes (circularity near 1). Widen the range and read the values output with 'Inspect CV Data' to calibrate; switch the property to aspect ratio / extent / solidity for other queries.\n- FILTER BY SIMILARITY: 'CV Select Contour' picks the largest blob as a reference and 'CV Filter Contours By Shape' (cv2.matchShapes, Hu moments - scale/rotation invariant) finds its lookalikes. Inspect the distances output to pick max_distance.\n- MERGE: 'CV Merge Contours' unites contours closer than 'gap' pixels - reunite a broken outline or treat a cluster as one object.\n- PAINT / USE AS MASK: the interiors are filled white onto a black 'CV Constant Like' canvas - that IS the mask: shown via 'CV Array -> Mask', and applied to the photo with cv2.bitwise_and.\n\nEverything stays NPARRAY between the converts; previews only render."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
